ComfyUI: make cache-key computation linear in the size of the workflow.

CacheKeySetInputSignature.get_node_signature built a node's key from a flat list of
every ancestor's immediate signature and hashed the whole list, for every node. That
is O(nodes * depth), paid on every prompt execution before any work begins. A straight
800-node chain spent 8.3 s there; 800 nodes with no depth took 18 ms.

Signatures are now built bottom-up and memoised: a node's key is its own inputs plus
the already-computed signature of each node it links to, shared by reference. The walk
is iterative so deep workflows cannot exhaust the stack, and the key is assembled
already-hashable because to_hashable does not recognise a frozenset and would other-
wise reduce every parent signature to an Unhashable sentinel.

Keys change shape. The caches are in-memory and rebuilt per prompt, so nothing
persistent depends on the old form. What must not change is which nodes are treated as
equal and which are invalidated when one changes; verify_comfy.py checks both.

  chain, 800 nodes:   8,312 ms -> 4.42 ms
  diamond, 800 nodes: 10,598 ms -> 4.66 ms
  wide, 800 nodes:       18.2 ms -> 4.32 ms
  drperf: 318.1*n_sq -> 0.351*n_sq

